  "scope": [
    "Generate ordinary task titles as Work Item ID, bounded short goal, Position, and Agent display name; define a separate project control-task convention.",
    "Add an explicit repository task-title refresh command and apply it to current registered tasks without changing thread identity, lifecycle authority, or archive state.",
    "Update the identity-free project overlay, self-host installation, operating documentation, ADR, and tests; rename only the currently accessible Codex tasks covered by the accepted convention."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "New work-item, handoff, orchestration, and task-registration suggestions use WI-#### · short goal · Position (Agent), with deterministic whitespace, delimiter, and length handling.",
    "The project-control convention is Project · control scope · Primary Position (Agent), while docs and policy make clear that titles are navigation labels and thread ID plus Work Item ID remain canonical.",
    "An explicit refresh operation updates stored suggestions idempotently, preserves all task/thread/status/model fields, and performs no Codex app mutation by itself.",
    "Current Temple registry suggestions and visible accessible task titles follow the accepted convention; tests, schema, Doctor, and Independent QA pass."
  ],
